### Later contract refinements

#### Booking qualification and email ownership

The [interface catalogue](../phase-1-architecture/contracts/INTERFACE_CATALOG.md#booking-qualification-and-email-review-navigation--2026-10-08)
now links four separate reviews for the existing booking routes:

| Definition | Current evidence |
|---|---|
| IF-BOOK-02 qualification control | [Correction-1 logical review](../phase-1-architecture/contracts/reviews/booking-qualification-admission-v1-2026-10-08.md): admission, email correction and historical outcomes. |
| IF-BOOK-02 qualification wire | [Correction-1 wire review](../../output/research/booking-qualification-wire-2026-10-08/final-independent-review.json): closed submission/reconciliation, safe responses and proposed HTTP/finite limits; schema and local mailbox observations only. |
| IF-BOOK-03/04 email ownership | [Correction-1 control/view review](../../output/research/booking-email-ownership-2026-10-08/final-independent-review.json): code verification, accessible extension, uncertain delivery and current email authority. The [visual explanation](definition-walkthrough.html#booking-email) has separate supplied source/pixel inspection. |
| IF-BOOK-03/04 email wire | [Correction-1 wire review](../../output/research/booking-email-wire-2026-10-08/final-independent-review.json): closed directions/current controls and protected extension work admission; validator evidence remains schema-only. |

All four have bounded PASS for their recorded frozen inputs. Later navigation
edits do not replace those inputs or extend their verdicts. The 32-slot combined
operation-record recommendation supersedes the qualification-only 16-slot profile
only when email controls are enabled; the separate protected work reservation is
an unmeasured proposal. No implemented booking, sent email, current provider
entitlement, measured capacity, full timing accessibility or integrated acceptance
is inferred. The later scheduling refinements below retain those same controls
and existing IF-BOOK-05/06/08/09 routes.

